<header><p class="st-kicker">crusader state · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Cyprus</h1><p class="st-meta">1192 CE – 1489 CE · capital Nicosia</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Crusader kingdom of the Lusignan dynasty that ruled Cyprus for three centuries, the last Latin outpost in the Levant after the fall of Acre.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1192 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-i-of-england">Richard I</a> sold <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a>, recently taken from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isaac-komnenos-of-cyprus">Isaac Komnenos</a> and returned by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-templar">Templars</a>, to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guy-of-lusignan">Guy of Lusignan</a>, the deposed king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>. Guy settled Frankish knights on the island. His brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aimery-of-cyprus">Aimery</a> obtained a crown from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-vi-holy-roman-emperor">Emperor Henry VI</a> and was crowned king in 1197.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>A French-speaking Catholic nobility ruled a mostly Greek <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> population, using the laws of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-jerusalem">Kingdom of Jerusalem</a> and a High Court of barons. The Orthodox church was subordinated to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a>. After the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acre">Acre</a> in 1291 <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/genoese-famagusta">Famagusta</a> became a great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/entrepot">entrepot</a> for Italian merchants. Gothic cathedrals in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicosia">Nicosia</a> and Famagusta and the abbey of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bellapais-abbey">Bellapais</a> survive. Peter I led a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a> that sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandria">Alexandria</a> in 1365.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-genoa">Genoa</a> seized <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/genoese-famagusta">Famagusta</a> in 1373, and a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> invasion in 1426 captured King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/janus-of-cyprus">Janus</a> and made the kingdom tributary to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-ii-of-cyprus">James II</a> married the Venetian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catherine-cornaro">Catherine Cornaro</a>; after his death she ruled as queen until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> forced her to abdicate in 1489, creating <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/venetian-cyprus">Venetian Cyprus</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-cyprus.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Cyprus" width="320" height="240"><figcaption>Image: Cattette · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Medieval_Cyprus.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1192 CE – 1489 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>crusader state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Nicosia</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Aimery of Lusignan, Peter I, Catherine Cornaro</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity (rulers), Eastern Orthodox Christianity (majority)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old French, Medieval Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/cyprus">Cyprus</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Lusignan Cyprus, Lordship of Cyprus</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1340&amp;focus=kingdom-of-cyprus" aria-label="Kingdom of Cyprus on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5525 906 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Cyprus lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5845 1162L5908 1277M5845 1162L5845 1162M5845 1162L5229 694M5845 1162L5815 1335M5845 1162L5845 1162M5845 1162L5860 1164"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5908 1277h0M5845 1162h0M5229 694h0M5815 1335h0M5845 1162h0M5860 1164h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5845 1162h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5845 1162h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Nicosia. <a href="/atlas?year=1340&amp;focus=kingdom-of-cyprus">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
